WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.612
The baseline check reports six rules.

2
00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:05.584
Two come straight from
Learn's hierarchy guidance:

3
00:00:05.584 --> 00:00:08.769
creating management groups
must need authorization,

4
00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:12.874
and new subscriptions must land in a
default group, not the tenant root.

5
00:00:12.874 --> 00:00:14.571
One is the program's design:

6
00:00:14.571 --> 00:00:18.425
the required assignments must
sit at the intermediate root.

7
00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:20.762
One is information, not a finding:

8
00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:25.175
an initiative in DoNotEnforce
is exactly what Step 1 intends.

9
00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:28.237
Then logs: every platform
resource must send

10
00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:31.050
an enabled log to the platform workspace.

11
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.938
And Defender for Cloud: the
required plans must be on Standard.

12
00:00:34.938 --> 00:00:38.300
The types and plans it checks
live in a configuration

13
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.400
file you change only in
a reviewed pull request.
